        "problem": "Evaluate ${}_{8}{C}_{8}.$",
        "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ and $r=8,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{8}{C}_{8} & =\\frac{8!}{(8-8)!\\,8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{0!\\,8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{8!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{8!}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
